{% comment -%}
A type's learner page, type/<name>/start.md, written from the type catalog (the spec is
Documentation/v0.2/type-reference-generation.md). Each fact comes from its one home: the type's description and guide
(type.guide.md, learner prose the builder never reads); each member's summary and call form from the member-name line
of <member>.notes.md; each argument's name and type from the catalog (member.Arguments), how a step says it and what
it changes from the argument's notes line; what a member returns from its notes' Returns line, else its type. Members
come in catalog order, arguments in their method's order. A property or a no-argument method has no argument table; the
call form's parentheses (or their absence) ride the member note's say form, which the catalog cannot tell apart.
Needs: type (one element of %!app.type.list%).
{%- endcomment -%}
# {{ type.Name }}
{{ type.Description | strip }}
{%- if type.Guide %}

{{ type.Guide | strip }}
{%- endif %}
{%- for m in type.Property %}
{%- assign note = m.Note %}
{%- assign self = note.Line | where: "Name", m.Name | first %}

## {{ m.Name }}
{{ self.Prose | strip }}
{%- if self.Say %}

`{{ self.Say }}`
{%- endif %}
{%- if m.Arguments.size > 0 %}

| Argument | How you say it | Type | Required | Default | What it changes |
|----------|----------------|------|----------|---------|-----------------|
{%- for a in m.Arguments %}
{%- assign line = note.Line | where: "Name", a.Name | first %}
| {{ a.Name }} | {{ line.Say }} | {{ a.Type.Name }} | {% if a.Required %}yes{% else %}no{% endif %} | {% if a.HasDefault %}{{ a.Default }}{% else %}—{% endif %} | {{ line.Prose }} |
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

**Returns:** {% if note.Returns %}{{ note.Returns.Prose }}{% else %}a `{{ m.Type.Name }}`.{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
